    "description": "HG-1-ML (AKM): Laffs Dynamics\n\nM-Lok handguard for the AKM platform. \n\n\n\nFilament Recommended: Nylon, Carbon Fiber Nylon, Glass Filled Nylon. \n\nPrint Settings:\n\nFirst Layer Print Height: .2mm \nStandard Layer Height: .16\nWall Thickness: .40 \nWall Perimeters: 7+\nInfill: 80%+\nSupport Material Percentage: 20%\n\n\n\nHardware: \n\n1x M4x10 Set Screw (Optional)\n\n\n\nNotes:\n\n1) For the love of fuck, just don't make me have to come through the monitor to slap you if you try printing this in something \nlike PLA+. The barrel gets hot as Satan's balls underneath the handguard. If you don't print it in something heat resistant like \nglass filled nylon, don't cry about it later when after only a mag or two, your handguard turns to melted mush. \n\n2) Should the pivot slightly up and down whilst locked into the front handguard retainer, install the set screw through the bottom \nof the picatinny rail, up against the bottom of the retainer. Do not overtighten. Just drive it until it makes contact with the retainer, \nand the handguard no longer moves. \n\n\n",
